WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.763
This code creates a small chain of calculations We
begin with sales and costs

00:00:06.684 --> 00:00:12.434
Profit is sales minus costs Tax is calculated from
profit and net profit

00:00:12.461 --> 00:00:18.108
is what remains after subtracting the tax Run the
example and follow

00:00:18.134 --> 00:00:23.900
the dependency from top to bottom The later values
depend on the earlier ones so

00:00:23.926 --> 00:00:29.876
the order of the statements matters Try changing the
tax rate from five percent

00:00:29.902 --> 00:00:35.457
to ten percent Profit should stay the same because
the profit calculation does not use

00:00:35.483 --> 00:00:40.483
the tax rate Tax and net profit should change
because they do depend on it

00:00:41.418 --> 00:00:46.010
This is a good way to practice reasoning about which
variables influence which results
